Seam: -[AppController application:openURLs:] in chrome/browser/app_controller_mac.mm,
      at the top of the method, before the StartupTabs it builds.
Why: a link another application hands the running browser opens in a small
     window of its own (R4.3), in the space a routing rule names, instead of
     a tab in whatever space happens to be on screen. Taken here because this
     is the only place macOS delivers such links, and declining is what keeps
     a cold launch, a `file:` URL and the `chromium://` scheme on Chromium's
     own path unchanged.
     No GN wiring: app_controller_mac.mm builds in //chrome/browser:core,
     which patch 0145 already gave a dep on //arcium/ui/browser.
Delegates to: arcium::OpenOutsideLinks

